---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import SiteHeader from "../components/SiteHeader.astro";
import SiteFooter from "../components/SiteFooter.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="About Us — VarianceCalc"
  description="VarianceCalc is a free, private, browser-based variance and standard deviation calculator. Learn why we built it and how it works."
  skipTo="main-content"
  breadcrumbs={[{ name: "About Us", path: "/about/" }]}
>
  <SiteHeader currentPath="/about/" />

  <main id="main-content">
    <section class="border-b border-hairline">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5 pt-16 pb-12 sm:px-6 sm:pt-20">
        <h1 class="text-4xl font-semibold tracking-[-0.03em] text-ink sm:text-5xl">About Us</h1>
        <p class="mt-5 max-w-xl text-base leading-relaxed text-body sm:text-lg">
          VarianceCalc is a small, focused tool built to make one job — calculating
          variance and standard deviation — fast, clear, and trustworthy.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="border-b border-hairline">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl space-y-6 px-5 py-14 text-base leading-relaxed text-body sm:px-6 sm:py-16">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink">Why we built this</h2>
        <p>
          Most online variance calculators either bury the answer behind ads and pop-ups,
          fail on messy real-world input like spreadsheet columns pasted with stray commas
          and currency symbols, or hide exactly how the result was computed. We wanted
          something different: paste your numbers, get an instant answer, and see every
          step of the math worked out on your own data — sample variance, population
          variance, standard deviation, mean, count, and sum of squares, all in one place.
        </p>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink">How it works</h2>
        <p>
          The entire calculator runs client-side in your browser using a small, typed
          statistics engine. Nothing you paste or type is ever uploaded to a server,
          logged, or stored — the only time your data touches a URL is if you explicitly
          click "Copy link" to share a result. There's no account and no installation,
          and your calculator data never leaves your browser.
        </p>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink">Who it's for</h2>
        <p>
          Students checking homework, teachers building examples, analysts who need a
          quick sanity check without opening a full statistics package, and anyone else
          who just wants a correct answer explained clearly. If you have feedback or spot
          something that looks wrong, we'd like to hear about it — see the
          <a href="/contact/" class="text-link hover:underline">Contact Us</a> page.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <SiteFooter />
</Layout>
